# Write clear summaries

A summary is the line under a title: a Civica page description, the helper text on a card, a hint under a field or a notification preview.

With the title, it says what the content covers, so people can tell at a glance if it is for them.

## Use clear and common language

Describe the content in plain words, from the reader’s side, so they can judge whether it applies to them.

Choose words [as you would for a title](clear-titles.html#use-clear-and-common-language). Use the summary for familiar words the title had no room for.

Those extra words also help people find the page when they search.

## Keep your summary short

Keep every summary to 160 characters or fewer, spaces included. That is roughly what a search result shows.

When a summary runs longer, someone who reads only the first 160 characters must still get the main point.

## Include punctuation

End with a full stop, so that a screen reader pauses before whatever comes next.

## Avoid redundant introductory words

Do not open by naming the kind of thing it is, such as “This card shows…” or “An automation that…”.

Spend the space on new words, not on words the title already has.

## Use active language

Every summary needs a verb, in the active voice.

Starting with “How…”, “What…” or “When…” is an easy way in, for example “What to check before you restore a backup.”

## Give help in the right place

<h3 id="wg-053">Put help beside the decision</h3>

Write the hint next to the field it explains, for example “How long the light stays on after the last movement.” Do not send people to another page to understand a field.

<h3 id="wg-055">Support learning without overloading the task</h3>

Give the one fact people need now, such as “A mains-powered Zigbee device usually passes messages on, so a Zigbee smart plug can help a distant sensor connect.” Offer more as a named link.

<h3 id="wg-056">Keep examples honest</h3>

Say when something is an example, and tell people what to use instead: “For example, `light.reading_lamp`. Use the entity ID of your own light.”
